WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.559 --> 00:00:04.720
As the summer movie season draws to a close,
Netflix is prepping a new batch of originals

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.331
that are just as good — if not better — than
anything you'll catch at a theater, along

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.080
with a lot of big-time movies and TV shows
you might have missed the first time around.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.260
Stock up on popcorn, because here's what you
can look forward to streaming on Netflix in

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:16.940
August.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.300
Wet Hot American Summer: Ten Years Later

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.600
Grab your gear and prepare for one more visit
to Camp Firewood.

00:00:22.609 --> 00:00:26.650
Most of the gang from the cult classic Wet
Hot American Summer returns for a sequel series

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:31.630
that picks up in 1991, a decade after the
events of the original movie and the 2015

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:32.440
prequel series.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.820
"What am I gonna miss my camp reunion?"

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.700
The eight-episode Wet Hot American Summer:
Ten Years Later will bring back a lot of its

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:43.260
originals as well as introduce some new faces,
so get ready to travel back in time to camp

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:44.040
on August 4th.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:45.840
"Ahh!"

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.780
Voltron: Legendary Defender (Season 3)

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.780
A new take on the classic Voltron series from
the '80s, Legendary Defender follows the pilots

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.920
of five mechanical lions who unite to form
the massive Voltron.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:02.080
But the third season of this revival will
find our heroes in a tricky situation.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:06.140
On one hand, they're still basking in the
glory of their victory over Emperor Zarkon.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:10.280
On the other, his son Prince Lotor is ready
to step into his villainous shoes.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.030
On top of all that, the Black Paladin Shiro
is nowhere to be found, which means the other

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:15.800
pilots can't form Voltron.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.060
"No black lion, no voltron."

00:01:19.649 --> 00:01:22.020
Does that mean Princess Allura could take
on a bigger role?

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.440
We'll find out when Season 3 of Voltron premieres
on August 4.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:26.720
Icarus

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.820
If you haven't yet heard enough about Russia
on the news lately, you're in luck.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:35.340
Icarus is a documentary that will delve into
the story of how dozens of Russian Olympians

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.990
were caught in a state-run doping program
designed to ensure the country would fare

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:41.440
well at the 2014 winter games in Sochi.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:46.619
The movie follows filmmaker and biker Bryan
Fogel as he attempts to beat anti-doping tests

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.480
and becomes mired in a conspiracy.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:53.140
Along the way, he befriends the man who runs
Russia's doping program, Dr. Grigory Rodchenkov,

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:56.689
who explains everything behind the scenes
— including that some of his colleagues

00:01:56.689 --> 00:01:58.300
have mysteriously vanished.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:03.040
The documentary, which premiered at the Sundance
Film Festival in January, lands on Netflix

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.000
on August 4.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:05.180
Naked

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.860
In this romantic comedy, Marlon Wayans finds
himself in his own version of Groundhog Day,

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:11.400
but with a revealing new twist.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.880
Instead of starting the day in bed, he continuously
wakes up naked in an elevator.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:20.600
Based on a Swedish film from 2000, the Americanized
update will be available to watch over and

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.220
over beginning August 11.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:23.760
Atypical

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.340
In this quirky new Netflix series, Jennifer
Jason Leigh stars as Elsa, the protective

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:33.100
mother of Sam, an autistic high school senior
who is navigating the transition into adulthood.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:37.220
His journey isn't easy, and it forces both
him and his mother to grapple with change

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.260
while Sam searches for love and independence.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.780
"Why does my to-do list say remove stick from
butt?

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:43.420
I don't know!"

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.720
Atypical premieres on the streaming service
on August 11th

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:48.580
The Defenders

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:53.200
The top draw of the month is The Defenders,
the long-awaited crossover miniseries that

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.780
ties together all four of Netflix's Marvel
shows.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:03:00.660
The Defenders will gather Jessica Jones, Daredevil,
Luke Cage, and Iron Fist as the street-level

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:05.129
heroes team up against a diabolical villain
named Alexandra — who may or may not be

00:03:05.129 --> 00:03:08.760
the leader of the mysterious and ancient organization
known as The Hand.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:10.940
"I'm not hugging you."

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:15.780
The first season consists of eight episodes,
all of which will be available to stream August

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:18.800
18th, so go ahead and cancel all your plans
for that weekend.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:20.640
This one'll be a must-watch.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.780
What Happened to Monday?

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:27.040
If you're not that interested in watching
small screen superheroes in action, another

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.500
option for August 18th will be the premiere
of What Happened to Monday?

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:34.629
This futuristic thriller film centers on a
family that gives birth to septuplets in a

00:03:34.629 --> 00:03:37.460
world where parents are only allowed to bear
one child each.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:42.220
For all seven sisters to survive, the family
will have to resort to extraordinary measures.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:46.160
The pic features Noomi Rapace as all seven
of the sisters, each named for the day of

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.340
the week on which they're allowed to go outside
under a shared identity.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:52.920
When one of the sisters goes missing, the
others must carefully comb the city for their

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.680
missing sibling before the government gets
their hands on her and exposes them all.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:01.660
This dystopian thriller appears to fall somewhere
in between TV's clone drama Orphan Black and

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:06.540
the Bourne Identity movies, so strap in for
a wild game of cat and mouse...well, okay,

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.040
mice.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:08.660
Death Note

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.239
What would you do if you stumbled across a
mysterious notebook that allows you to kill

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.920
anyone you want just by writing their name
in it?

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.920
You probably shouldn't sell it on Amazon.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:23.040
Based on the iconic manga series that first
debuted in 2003, the Netflix original movie

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:27.169
Death Note tells the story of Light Turner,
a Seattle high school student who comes to

00:04:27.169 --> 00:04:31.560
possess a notebook dropped to Earth by Ryuk,
a god of death who handles all the murdering.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:32.960
"Shall we begin?"

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:37.660
Turner decides to use the notebook to become
a vigilante, but his run might not last long.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.660
A detective named L is determined to uncover
the source behind the killings.

00:04:41.669 --> 00:04:45.600
Death Note premieres August 25, and from the
looks of the the trailer, it's definitely

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:46.420
worth a watch.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.020
Disjointed

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:53.340
This new Netflix Original sitcom stars Kathy
Bates as a lifelong advocate for marijuana

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:57.830
legalization who finally lives out her dream
as the owner of a cannabis dispensary in Los

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:58.330
Angeles.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:02.280
Chuck Lorre, who brought The Big Bang Theory
and Two and a Half Men to CBS, co-created

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.470
the series with former Daily Show head writer
David Javerbaum, so prepare to find yourself

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:09.620
in a cloud of small screen smoke starting
on August 25th.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:11.660
New movies

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:16.880
Netflix is exponentially increasing its Keanu
factor in August, with all three installments

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:19.700
of the Matrix trilogy hitting the service
on August 1st.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.700
But if you're in the mood for action with
a little less social commentary, you can watch

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:27.900
Will Smith battle a giant mechanical spider
in Wild Wild West that same day.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.930
For those who love drama, The Founder is a
must-watch.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:35.150
It stars Michael Keaton as McDonald's creator
Ray Kroc in this captivating biopic that hits

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.480
Netflix on August 2nd.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:41.840
Netflix will also add Gold, the recent crime
drama starring a very bald Matthew McConaughey,

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:42.720
on August 16th.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:46.920
If you're looking for something a little more
high-brow, however, the documentary drop is

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.440
pretty solid for the month as well.

00:05:48.789 --> 00:05:52.340
The critically acclaimed Barbecue, which is
about barbecue culture in different countries,

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:53.840
comes online August 15th.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:59.000
And Feel Rich: Health Is the New Wealth, from
executive producer Quincy Jones, centers on

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.319
a revolutionary shift in hip-hop culture from
overindulgence to maintaining a healthier

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.920
lifestyle, and will be available August 23rd.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:11.000
More vintage new releases for the month include
Jackie Brown and I Am Sam, while more recent

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:14.919
little-seen films like Cloud Atlas and Beautiful
Creatures will also be available for your

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.180
streaming pleasure this month.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.610
As for those with kiddos, not to worry.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:22.280
There'll be plenty of new family-friendly
fodder available in August as well, including

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:24.660
Sing, Holes, and A Cinderella Story.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:28.500
After the little ones go to bed, though, be
sure to check out the newest thriller options

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:33.479
on the site, including The Astronaut's Wife,
Funny Games, and The Number 23, all of which

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.160
arrive on August 1st.

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:36.700
New television

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:41.300
As always, there's a new batch of TV shows
to catch up with — or suddenly become addicted

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.160
to — in August.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:46.300
If you haven't gotten enough of the Medellin
drug cartel thanks to Narcos, the first season

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.900
of Surviving Escobar will launch on the first
of the month.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:53.419
Meanwhile, the sixth season of ABC's Once
Upon a Time will drop on August 25th, helping

00:06:53.419 --> 00:06:57.550
catch you up on all the Storybrooke shenanigans
before the seventh season reboots the show

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.240
into unknown magical territory this fall.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.720
"Trust me I've done you a favor.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:05.040
All magic comes with a price."

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:09.780
And if you didn't catch the first season of
NBC's hit new sitcom The Good Place, well…

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.460
"Somebody royally forked up."

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:16.660
Be sure to circle August 25th on your calendar,
because it's well worth your time.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.540
"Do you have a second to eat my farts?"

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:20.040
"Ohhhh"

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:21.340
Thanks for watching!

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.960
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:23.979 --> 00:07:26.270
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

